hi my name is Silvia you I'm the  chef/owner of churro borough here in Los  Angeles this has been a project long in  the making  I had gone to culinary school in New  York and came back to Los Angeles and  decided that instead of working in  another restaurant I wanted to do  something for myself  so for me you know I thought of it more  like what are components that go really  well together a lot of times you want  something that's warm and cold and  something with texture to something  that's smooth and so kind of digging  into my memories and things like that  the churro kind of came up in my head  more often than once it has that crispy  factor that flaky factor is a lightness  to it but I thought you know what a  heaviness to it as well and it balances  and pairs really well with ice creams  and so one day I decided to make some  trails from my family and decided to put  a scoop of ice cream on and it tasted  really good and after weeks and months  of just research and development the  true ice cream santa came about we make  everything in-house a small batch from  scratch it really ensures the quality  and the freshness of what we do
 

